.TH XLS 1 "2026" "xls 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xls \- a terminal spreadsheet for XLS, XLSX and CSV files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xls
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xls
reads and writes Excel \fB.xls\fR (BIFF8), \fB.xlsx\fR (OOXML) and \fB.csv\fR
files, evaluates Excel formulas with a built\-in engine, and provides an
interactive terminal UI. With no subcommand and a terminal attached, the given
\fIFILE\fR is opened in the interactive editor.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B open \fIFILE\fR
Open \fIFILE\fR in the interactive TUI.
.TP
.B info \fIFILE\fR
Print metadata: format, sheets, dimensions and date system.
.TP
.B get \fIFILE\fR [\fISHEET\fR!]\fICELL\fR
Print a cell's displayed value, e.g. \fBxls get book.xlsx Sheet1!B2\fR.
.TP
.B set \fIFILE\fR [\fISHEET\fR!]\fICELL\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Set a cell (number, text or \fB=\fR formula), recalculate and save.
.TP
.B eval \fIFILE\fR \fIFORMULA\fR
Evaluate a formula against the file's data and print the result.
.TP
.B export \fIFILE\fR \-\-format csv|xlsx|xls [\-\-sheet \fINAME\fR] [\-\-out \fIPATH\fR] [\-\-stream]
Convert between formats. With \fB\-\-stream\fR (csv/tsv/jsonl output, xlsx/csv
input) rows are streamed without loading the whole workbook into memory \(em for
files too large to fit in RAM. Streaming uses cached formula values.
.TP
.B import \fICSV\fR \-\-into \fITARGET\fR [\-\-sheet \fINAME\fR]
Add a CSV as a sheet in an existing or new workbook.
.TP
.B name list|add|rm \fIFILE\fR ...
Manage defined names (named ranges): list them, add/replace one
(\fBadd\fR \fINAME\fR \fIREFERS_TO\fR [\fB\-\-sheet\fR \fIS\fR]), or remove one.
.TP
.B table list|add|rm \fIFILE\fR ...
Manage Excel table objects: list them, create one over a range
(\fBadd\fR \fIRANGE\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-header\fR]), or remove one.
Tables support structured references in formulas (e.g. \fISales[Amount]\fR).
.TP
.B diff \fIFILE1\fR \fIFILE2\fR
Print a cell\-by\-cell diff; exit status 1 if differences are found.
.SH "STDIN"
A \fIFILE\fR of \fB-\fR reads CSV from standard input, e.g.
\fBcat data.csv | xls eval - '=SUM(A:A)'\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-password \fIPASSWORD\fR
Decrypt a password\-protected workbook (ECMA\-376 agile or standard encryption).
Without it, an encrypted file is reported with its scheme. Accepted by any
subcommand. Editing an encrypted file and saving writes an unencrypted copy.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH "INTERACTIVE KEYS"
Arrows/Tab/Enter navigate; Shift+Arrow selects; F2 or typing edits; Enter/Tab
commits and recalculates; Ctrl+S saves; Ctrl+Z/Ctrl+Y undo/redo;
Ctrl+C/X/V copy/cut/paste; Ctrl+G go to cell; Ctrl+F find; \fB:\fR command
palette; \fBq\fR quits.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success, 1 on error or (for \fBdiff\fR) when differences are found.
